AgentDeobfBench — CodeNet100 reference benchmark
================================================

Program text and test cases
---------------------------

Source: IBM Project CodeNet, https://github.com/IBM/Project_CodeNet

Paper: Puri et al., "Project CodeNet: A Large-Scale AI for Code Dataset for
Learning a Diversity of Coding Tasks", NeurIPS 2021 Datasets and Benchmarks.

License: Community Data License Agreement — Permissive — Version 2.0
(CDLA-Permissive-2.0), https://cdla.dev/permissive-2-0/

This release uses Project CodeNet data, not its Apache-2.0 tooling. The original
programs, input/expected-output test cases, generated protected programs, and
deobfuscation outputs retain the applicable data terms. Redistributions must
retain this notice and license link.

Selection and comparison
------------------------

The reference selection follows JsDeObsBench:
https://github.com/Ch3nYe/JsDeObsBench, reviewed at commit
8b2e1c35dc4ae25a46ea580ea5dcb6b5de5edbe9 (2025-07-26).

Paper: Chen, Jin, and Lin, "JsDeObsBench: Measuring and Benchmarking LLMs for
JavaScript Deobfuscation", ACM CCS 2025, doi:10.1145/3719027.3744871

That repository's reviewed snapshot contained no root LICENSE. Consequently,
this release vendors no JsDeObsBench implementation code. `selection.json` and
`sample_ids.jsonl` record factual selection and ordering metadata for
reproducibility; the selected program text remains Project CodeNet data under
the terms above.

AgentDeobfBench artifacts
-------------------------

The protected builds, metadata, released predictions, aggregation scripts, and
documentation were produced for AgentDeobfBench. The root MIT license covers
repository-authored code and documentation but does not replace the Project
CodeNet data terms.
